{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"5a07920e-eaea-4f9a-a883-1f9c06269754","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I implemented `slugify` in `textutil.py`, and `cx-route test` now passes.\n\n**What changed**\n- [textutil.py:3](file:///root/.cx-wt/textutil-live-agy-1/textutil.py#L3): added `import re`.\n- [textutil.py:12](file:///root/.cx-wt/textutil-live-agy-1/textutil.py#L12): replaced `raise NotImplementedError` with `return re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \"-\", text.lower()).strip(\"-\")`. It lowercases the text, turns every run of anything other than ASCII letters and digits into a single hyphen, and removes hyphens at the start and end. This is what the docstring describes.\n\n**What I ran**\n- `cx-route test`: 3 tests ran, all passed.\n- `git status`: only `textutil.py` is modified. I didn't touch the tests.\n\n**Open issues:** None.\n\nDIGEST: Implemented slugify in textutil.py with a single regex and `cx-route test` passes (3/3) with the tests unchanged.\n","duration_seconds":18.195675741,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":10122,"output_tokens":1334,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":64862,"total_tokens":11456}}}
